  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Traditional music of the Khasi of the Meghalaya hills is led at dance festivals such as Shad Suk Mynsiem and Shad Nongkrem by the tangmuri shawm over ksing drums, while songs are accompanied by the duitara plucked lute and the besli flute; men chant phawar couplets during the dances. The kuzhal card stands in for the tangmuri, the generic drum for the ksing, the dotara card for the duitara and the flute card for the besli.",
